    "title": "Help & Support",
    "contactUs": "Contact Support",
    "contactSubtitle": "Have questions or feedback about LifeLink? Reach out to our support team.",
    "emailSupport": "Email Support",
    "faqTitle": "Frequently Asked Questions",
    "faqQuestion1": "Who can donate blood?",
    "faqAnswer1": "Anyone aged 18-65, weighing over 50kg, and in good general health with no active infections can donate.",
    "faqQuestion2": "How often can I donate?",
    "faqAnswer2": "You can safely donate whole blood once every 90 days (3 months) to allow your body to fully replenish iron levels.",
    "faqQuestion3": "Is my personal data secure?",
    "faqAnswer3": "Yes, your contact details are encrypted and only shown to verified requesters when you explicitly choose to respond to a request.",
    "faqQuestion4": "How do I request blood?",
    "faqAnswer4": "Navigate to the 'Request' tab, fill in the patient details, select the blood type and hospital, and submit. Matched donors nearby will be notified."
